#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Turn memory pressure into a level (normal, slow, pause) for heavy-build.

    pressure-coordinator             run for good, one sample every 5 s
    pressure-coordinator --once      take two samples 5 s apart and print them
    pressure-coordinator --self-test run the built-in tests in a sandbox

Runs as pressure-coordinator.service, a systemd user unit in background.slice.
It only reads /proc and the cgroup tree and writes its own files. It never
kills, stops, freezes or signals any process, and it changes no cgroup limit.

Files it writes:

  ~/.local/state/pressure/level   one line, rewritten every sample (temp + mv):
      level=slow since=<epoch> updated=<epoch> reason="memory full avg10 6.1%"
      top=claude-123.scope:8.2%
    heavy-build counts it as slow when updated is 30 s to 10 min old, and
    ignores it after that or when updated is in the future.
  ~/.local/state/pressure/log     each level change, and one sample a minute.
    Cut to its last half when it passes log_max_bytes.
  $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/heavy-build.hold.pressure
    Only at pause: "expires=<now + 30> pressure-coordinator: level pause (...)",
    refreshed every sample and removed when the level drops below pause. A
    stop or restart leaves it; it runs out at its expires=. This is its own
    file. The manager's heavy-build.hold is never read, written or removed here.

On start it takes over the level in the level file when that was updated less
than 60 s ago (resume_secs), so a restart keeps slow or pause. An updated= in
the future is stale. Timers run on monotonic time, so a wall clock jump does
not move them. A gap between samples of more than 3 intervals starts the calm
count again. The config file is read again when it changes; a file with NaN,
infinity, a negative value or an out-of-range interval or hold_ttl_secs is
rejected as a whole (event=conf-rejected) and the last good config stays.

Signals (each sample):
  - memory PSI full avg10, system wide (/proc/pressure/memory);
  - memory PSI some and full avg10 of each child of claude.slice, app.slice and
    session.slice. A child whose memory.events "high" or "max" counter rose in
    the last 60 s is skipped: it is held back by its own MemoryHigh or
    MemoryMax, not by the machine. (On 2026-10-21 one Chrome unit at its own
    MemoryHigh made app.slice look stressed and blocked every build.)
  - disk swap-in (pswpin), zswap loads (zswpin), swap-out (pswpout), major
    faults (pgmajfault) and zswap writeback (zswpwb), per second over the
    last 60 s; zswpin is only logged;
  - memory.swap.current against memory.swap.max of claude.slice and
    builds.slice, when that max is a number;
  - io PSI full avg10;
  - MemAvailable, and swap room: 90% of SwapTotal minus swap used.

Thresholds (defaults; each is settable in ~/.config/pressure-coordinator.conf
as key=value, keys as in DEFAULTS below). From the 2026-10-21 swap-aware
redesign, section 4:

  slow  when any of these holds for enter_secs (15 s):
          memory full avg10 >= 2%           (slow_mem_full)
          a session's memory some avg10 >= 10%   (slow_scope_some)
          disk swap-in >= 2000 pages/s      (slow_swapin)
          swap room < 24 GiB                (slow_swap_room_gib)
  pause when any of these holds for enter_secs:
          memory full avg10 >= 5%           (pause_mem_full), only while
                                    MemAvailable < 10 GiB (pause_mem_full_avail_gib);
                                    with more free it caps at slow
          2 sessions' memory full avg10 >= 10% at once
                                    (pause_scope_full, pause_scope_count);
                                    one session alone only counts for slow
          disk swap-in >= 8000 pages/s      (pause_swapin)
          MemAvailable < 2 GiB              (pause_mem_avail_gib)
        and at once (no wait) when swap room < 12 GiB (pause_swap_room_gib),
        or when claude.slice or builds.slice uses 90% of its memory.swap.max
        (slice_swap_pct).

  One level down only after leave_secs (60 s) in which every signal of the
  current level stayed under half its enter threshold (MemAvailable over twice
  its threshold, or over recover_mem_avail_gib when that is above 0) and swap
  room stayed over 32 GiB (recover_swap_room_gib), and no trigger of a higher
  level held.

  recover_mem_avail_gib (default 0) sets the MemAvailable bar for leaving
  pause. 0 keeps twice pause_mem_avail_gib (4 GiB with the defaults). Set it
  lower on a machine that runs with little MemAvailable for hours and no other
  pressure, so pause does not hold on MemAvailable alone. The reason then reads
  "under the recovery bar: MemAvailable 2.1 GiB, needs 2.5".

One change from the design: it named pgmajfault over 1000/s (slow) and
4000/s (pause). Measured on 2026-10-22 at 09:01, ten minutes after a reboot,
pgmajfault ran at 1150/s while disk swap-in was 4 pages/s and memory full
was 0.5%: most major faults were page cache reads by builds, not swap. So
disk swap-in pages (pswpin) are the trigger, and pgmajfault is only logged
unless slow_majfault or pause_majfault is set above 0. zswap hits do not
count in pswpin, so pswpin is real disk reads. io PSI and zswap writeback are
logged only (slow_io_full and pause_io_full are 0, meaning off).

Second change, 2026-10-22: memory full avg10 alone pauses only while
MemAvailable is under pause_mem_full_avail_gib (10 GiB). Between 09:00 and
11:00 that day it paused 6 times on memory full 6.9% to 12% with 12 to 28 GiB
available. The stalls came from resting Claude sessions faulting their pages
back from zswap and disk swap (majfault 1.7k to 4.2k/s, zswpin 3k to 5.5k/s),
not from a shortage, and each pause held new builds 5 to 7 minutes. Above the
threshold the same signal gives slow, with the reason "memory full avg10 6.9%
but 25 GiB free, capped at slow". The leave test uses twice the threshold, as
for pause_mem_avail_gib. 0 turns the cap off (memory full pauses at any
MemAvailable). Every other pause trigger is unchanged.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import math
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import sys
import tempfile
import time
from collections import deque
from pathlib import Path

DEFAULTS: dict[str, float] = {
    "interval": 5,
    "enter_secs": 15,
    "leave_secs": 60,
    "rate_window_secs": 60,
    "own_limit_secs": 60,
    "slow_mem_full": 2,
    "pause_mem_full": 5,
    "pause_mem_full_avail_gib": 10,
    "slow_scope_some": 10,
    "pause_scope_full": 10,
    "pause_scope_count": 2,
    "slice_swap_pct": 90,
    "resume_secs": 60,
    "slow_swapin": 2000,
    "pause_swapin": 8000,
    "slow_majfault": 0,
    "pause_majfault": 0,
    "slow_io_full": 0,
    "pause_io_full": 0,
    "slow_swap_room_gib": 24,
    "pause_swap_room_gib": 12,
    "pause_mem_avail_gib": 2,
    # MemAvailable needed to leave pause; 0 means twice pause_mem_avail_gib
    # (the old behaviour).
    "recover_mem_avail_gib": 0,
    "recover_swap_room_gib": 32,
    "hold_ttl_secs": 30,
    "sample_log_secs": 60,
    "log_max_bytes": 5_000_000,
}
LEVELS = ("normal", "slow", "pause")
SLICES = ("claude.slice", "app.slice", "session.slice")
SWAP_SLICES = ("claude.slice", "builds.slice")
GIB = 1024**3


# Keys that must be over 0 (the rest may be 0, which turns a threshold off).
POSITIVE = ("interval", "rate_window_secs", "hold_ttl_secs", "log_max_bytes")


def check_conf(cfg: dict[str, float]) -> list[str]:
    """What is wrong with cfg: NaN, infinity, a negative number, 0 where it
    must be over 0, or a value that would break the loop or the hold."""
    errs: list[str] = []
    for k, v in cfg.items():
        if not math.isfinite(v) or v < 0:
            errs.append(f"{k}={v}")
        elif k in POSITIVE and v <= 0:
            errs.append(f"{k}={v} (must be over 0)")
    if not errs:
        if cfg["interval"] < 1 or cfg["interval"] > 60:
            errs.append(f"interval={cfg['interval']} (1 to 60)")
        if cfg["hold_ttl_secs"] > 600:
            errs.append(
                f"hold_ttl_secs={cfg['hold_ttl_secs']} (heavy-build trusts at most 600)"
            )
        if cfg["pause_scope_count"] < 1:
            errs.append(f"pause_scope_count={cfg['pause_scope_count']} (at least 1)")
    return errs


def read_conf(path: Path) -> tuple[dict[str, float], list[str]]:
    """DEFAULTS with numbers from key=value lines in path, and the list of
    problems. Unknown keys are skipped. A value that is not a number, or that
    check_conf rejects, is a problem: the caller then keeps its last good config."""
    cfg = dict(DEFAULTS)
    errs: list[str] = []
    try:
        text = path.read_text()
    except OSError:
        return cfg, errs
    for line in text.splitlines():
        line = line.split("#", 1)[0].strip()
        if "=" not in line:
            continue
        k, v = (s.strip() for s in line.split("=", 1))
        if k in cfg:
            try:
                cfg[k] = float(v)
            except ValueError:
                errs.append(f"{k}={v!r} is not a number")
    return cfg, errs + check_conf(cfg)


def psi(path: Path) -> tuple[float, float]:
    """(some avg10, full avg10) of a pressure file, (-1, -1) when unreadable."""
    some = full = -1.0
    try:
        for line in path.read_text().splitlines():
            m = re.match(r"(some|full) avg10=([0-9.]+)", line)
            if m:
                if m.group(1) == "some":
                    some = float(m.group(2))
                else:
                    full = float(m.group(2))
    except OSError:
        pass
    return some, full


def kv_file(path: Path) -> dict[str, int]:
    out: dict[str, int] = {}
    try:
        for line in path.read_text().splitlines():
            parts = line.split()
            if len(parts) >= 2 and parts[1].isdigit():
                out[parts[0].rstrip(":")] = int(parts[1])
    except OSError:
        pass
    return out


class Coordinator:
    """Timers (enter, leave, rates, own-limit) run on monotonic time, passed
    as mono. Wall time (now) is only written to files: since=, updated= and
    the hold's expires=. Without mono, now is used for both (the self-test)."""

    def __init__(
        self,
        cfg: dict[str, float],
        proc: Path,
        usvc: Path,
        state_dir: Path,
        run_dir: Path,
    ) -> None:
        self.cfg = cfg
        self.proc = proc
        self.usvc = usvc
        self.state_dir = state_dir
        self.level_file = state_dir / "level"
        self.log_file = state_dir / "log"
        self.hold_file = run_dir / "heavy-build.hold.pressure"
        self.level = 0
        self.since = 0.0
        self.above_since: dict[int, float | None] = {1: None, 2: None}
        self.calm_since: float | None = None
        self.last_mono: float | None = None
        self.counters: deque[tuple[float, dict[str, int]]] = deque()
        self.events: dict[str, tuple[int, float]] = {}
        self.last_sample_log = -1e18
        self.reason = ""

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ restart

    def resume(self, now: float) -> str:
        """Takes over the level of a coordinator that ran until less than
        resume_secs ago (its level file's updated=), so a restart does not drop
        a slow or pause level, and leaves the pressure hold in place. An
        updated= in the future, or older, is stale: start at normal.
        Returns what it did, for the start log line."""
        try:
            line = self.level_file.read_text()
        except OSError:
            return "level=normal resumed=no reason=no-level-file"
        m = re.search(r"(?:^|\s)level=(normal|slow|pause)(?:\s|$)", line)
        u = re.search(r"(?:^|\s)updated=(\d{1,15})(?:\s|$)", line)
        sm = re.search(r"(?:^|\s)since=(\d{1,15})(?:\s|$)", line)
        if not m or not u:
            return "level=normal resumed=no reason=unreadable-level-file"
        age = now - int(u.group(1))
        if age < -5:
            return f"level=normal resumed=no reason=updated-in-future age_s={age:.0f}"
        if age > self.cfg["resume_secs"]:
            return f"level=normal resumed=no reason=stale age_s={age:.0f}"
        self.level = LEVELS.index(m.group(1))
        self.since = float(sm.group(1)) if sm else now
        rm = re.search(r'reason="([^"]*)"', line)
        self.reason = "resumed: " + (rm.group(1) if rm else "")
        return f"level={LEVELS[self.level]} resumed=yes age_s={age:.0f}"

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ sampling

    def scopes(self, mono: float) -> tuple[float, float, str, int, int]:
        """Highest some and full avg10 over children of the session slices that
        are not at their own limit, the name of the top one, and how many are
        at or over pause_scope_full, and over half of it."""
        best_some = best_full = 0.0
        top = ""
        nfull = nhalf = 0
        seen: set[str] = set()
        for sl in SLICES:
            try:
                kids = [p for p in (self.usvc / sl).iterdir() if p.is_dir()]
            except OSError:
                continue
            for kid in kids:
                key = str(kid)
                seen.add(key)
                ev = kv_file(kid / "memory.events")
                n = ev.get("high", 0) + ev.get("max", 0)
                old = self.events.get(key)
                rose_at = old[1] if old else -1e18
                if old is not None and n > old[0]:
                    rose_at = mono
                self.events[key] = (n, rose_at)
                if mono - rose_at < self.cfg["own_limit_secs"]:
                    continue
                some, full = psi(kid / "memory.pressure")
                th = self.cfg["pause_scope_full"]
                if th > 0 and full >= th:
                    nfull += 1
                if th > 0 and full >= th / 2:
                    nhalf += 1
                if some > best_some or full > best_full:
                    if max(some, full) > max(best_some, best_full):
                        top = f"{kid.name}:{max(some, full):.1f}%"
                    best_some = max(best_some, some)
                    best_full = max(best_full, full)
        for key in list(self.events):
            if key not in seen:
                del self.events[key]
        return best_some, best_full, top, nfull, nhalf

    def slice_swap(self) -> tuple[str, float]:
        """The SWAP_SLICES slice whose memory.swap.current is nearest its
        memory.swap.max (when that is a number over 0), as "name:cur/max GiB",
        and that use in percent. ("-", 0) when none has a limit."""
        worst, pct = "-", 0.0
        for sl in SWAP_SLICES:
            try:
                mx = (self.usvc / sl / "memory.swap.max").read_text().strip()
                cur = int((self.usvc / sl / "memory.swap.current").read_text())
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                continue
            if not mx.isdigit() or int(mx) <= 0:
                continue
            p = 100.0 * cur / int(mx)
            if p >= pct:
                worst, pct = f"{sl}:{cur / GIB:.1f}/{int(mx) / GIB:.1f}GiB", p
        return worst, pct

    def sample(self, mono: float) -> dict[str, float | str]:
        cfg = self.cfg
        _, mem_full = psi(self.proc / "pressure/memory")
        _, io_full = psi(self.proc / "pressure/io")
        vm = kv_file(self.proc / "vmstat")
        mi = kv_file(self.proc / "meminfo")
        cnt = {
            k: vm.get(k, 0)
            for k in ("pswpin", "pswpout", "pgmajfault", "zswpwb", "zswpin")
        }
        self.counters.append((mono, cnt))
        while (
            len(self.counters) > 2
            and mono - self.counters[1][0] >= cfg["rate_window_secs"]
        ):
            self.counters.popleft()
        t0, c0 = self.counters[0]
        dt = mono - t0

        def rate(k: str) -> float:
            return max(0.0, (cnt[k] - c0[k]) / dt) if dt > 0 else 0.0

        sw_total = mi.get("SwapTotal", 0) * 1024
        sw_used = sw_total - mi.get("SwapFree", 0) * 1024
        scope_some, scope_full, top, nfull, nhalf = self.scopes(mono)
        sl_name, sl_pct = self.slice_swap()
        return {
            "mem_full": max(mem_full, 0.0),
            "io_full": max(io_full, 0.0),
            "scope_some": scope_some,
            "scope_full": scope_full,
            "scope_full_n": nfull,
            "scope_half_n": nhalf,
            "top": top or "-",
            "swapin": rate("pswpin"),
            "zswpin": rate("zswpin"),
            "swapout": rate("pswpout"),
            "majfault": rate("pgmajfault"),
            "zswpwb": rate("zswpwb"),
            "mem_avail_gib": mi.get("MemAvailable", 0) / 1048576,
            "swap_used_gib": sw_used / GIB,
            # No swap at all counts as plenty of room.
            "swap_room_gib": (0.9 * sw_total - sw_used) / GIB if sw_total else 1e9,
            "slice_swap": sl_name,
            "slice_swap_pct": sl_pct,
        }

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ levels

    def at_once(self, s: dict[str, float | str]) -> list[str]:
        """Pause triggers that act on the first sample, with no enter wait:
        global swap room under pause_swap_room_gib, or claude.slice or
        builds.slice swap use at slice_swap_pct of its memory.swap.max."""
        c = self.cfg
        out: list[str] = []
        room = float(s["swap_room_gib"])
        if room < c["pause_swap_room_gib"]:
            out.append(f"swap room {room:.1f} GiB")
        th = c["slice_swap_pct"]
        if th > 0 and float(s["slice_swap_pct"]) >= th:
            out.append(
                f"{s['slice_swap']} swap {float(s['slice_swap_pct']):.0f}% of its max"
            )
        return out

    def triggers(
        self, s: dict[str, float | str], lvl: int, scale: float = 1.0
    ) -> list[str]:
        """The enter conditions of level lvl that hold. scale 0.5 asks
        "is any signal at half its threshold or more" for the leave test.
        Per-scope pressure: one scope's some avg10 counts for slow; pause
        needs pause_scope_count (2) scopes at pause_scope_full at once, so one
        stalled session cannot pause every build."""
        c = self.cfg
        p = "slow" if lvl == 1 else "pause"
        out: list[str] = []

        def ge(sig: str, key: str, label: str, unit: str) -> None:
            th = c[key]
            v = float(s[sig])
            if th > 0 and v >= th * scale:
                out.append(f"{label} {v:.1f}{unit}")

        avail = float(s["mem_avail_gib"])
        # Memory full with plenty of MemAvailable is pages faulting back from
        # swap, not a shortage: it pauses only under pause_mem_full_avail_gib
        # (twice that in the leave test), and caps at slow above it.
        cap = c["pause_mem_full_avail_gib"]
        capped = cap > 0 and avail >= cap / scale
        if lvl == 2:
            if not capped:
                ge("mem_full", "pause_mem_full", "memory full avg10", "%")
        else:
            mf = float(s["mem_full"])
            pth = c["pause_mem_full"]
            if scale >= 1 and capped and pth > 0 and mf >= pth:
                out.append(
                    f"memory full avg10 {mf:.1f}% but {avail:.0f} GiB free, capped at slow"
                )
            else:
                ge("mem_full", "slow_mem_full", "memory full avg10", "%")
        if lvl == 1:
            ge(
                "scope_some",
                "slow_scope_some",
                f"{str(s['top']).split(':')[0]} some avg10",
                "%",
            )
        else:
            n = int(s["scope_full_n" if scale >= 1 else "scope_half_n"])
            if c["pause_scope_full"] > 0 and n >= c["pause_scope_count"]:
                out.append(
                    f"{n} scopes at full avg10 >= {c['pause_scope_full'] * scale:.0f}%"
                    f" (top {s['top']})"
                )
        ge("swapin", f"{p}_swapin", "disk swap-in", " pages/s")
        ge("majfault", f"{p}_majfault", "major faults", "/s")
        ge("io_full", f"{p}_io_full", "io full avg10", "%")
        room = float(s["swap_room_gib"])
        if scale < 1:
            if room <= c["recover_swap_room_gib"]:
                out.append(f"swap room {room:.1f} GiB")
            th = c["slice_swap_pct"]
            if lvl == 2 and th > 0 and float(s["slice_swap_pct"]) >= th * 0.9:
                out.append(
                    f"{s['slice_swap']} swap {float(s['slice_swap_pct']):.0f}% of its max"
                )
        elif room < c[f"{p}_swap_room_gib"]:
            out.append(f"swap room {room:.1f} GiB")
        if lvl == 2:
            if scale >= 1:
                out += [t for t in self.at_once(s) if not t.startswith("swap room")]
            bar = c["recover_mem_avail_gib"]
            if scale < 1 and bar > 0:
                if avail < bar:
                    out.append(
                        f"under the recovery bar: MemAvailable {avail:.1f} GiB,"
                        f" needs {bar:g}"
                    )
            elif avail < c["pause_mem_avail_gib"] / scale:
                out.append(f"MemAvailable {avail:.1f} GiB")
        return out

    def step(
        self, mono: float, s: dict[str, float | str], now: float | None = None
    ) -> str | None:
        """Moves the level for sample s. Returns the old level name when it changed."""
        c = self.cfg
        now = mono if now is None else now
        # A gap in sampling (suspend, a stuck process) proves nothing about
        # the time in between: the calm count starts again.
        if self.last_mono is not None and mono - self.last_mono > 3 * c["interval"]:
            self.calm_since = None
        self.last_mono = mono
        hot = {lvl: self.triggers(s, lvl) for lvl in (1, 2)}
        for lvl in (1, 2):
            if hot[lvl]:
                if self.above_since[lvl] is None:
                    self.above_since[lvl] = mono
            else:
                self.above_since[lvl] = None
        old = self.level
        target = 0
        for lvl in (2, 1):
            since = self.above_since[lvl]
            if lvl <= self.level or since is None:
                continue
            if (lvl == 2 and self.at_once(s)) or mono - since >= c["enter_secs"]:
                target = lvl
                break
        if target > self.level:
            self.level = target
            self.calm_since = None
            self.reason = "; ".join(hot[target])
        elif self.level > 0:
            warm = self.triggers(s, self.level, 0.5)
            # Never drop while a higher level's trigger holds, even one that
            # has not held for enter_secs yet (MemAvailable falling at slow).
            higher = [t for lvl in range(self.level + 1, 3) for t in hot[lvl]]
            if warm or higher:
                self.calm_since = None
                cur = hot[self.level] or higher or warm
                if hot[self.level] or higher:
                    self.reason = "; ".join(cur)
                else:
                    # The recovery bar is its own number, not half of one.
                    half = [t for t in cur if not t.startswith("under the recovery")]
                    bar = [t for t in cur if t.startswith("under the recovery")]
                    self.reason = "; ".join(
                        (["still over half: " + "; ".join(half)] if half else [])
                        + bar
                    )
            else:
                if self.calm_since is None:
                    self.calm_since = mono
                calm = mono - self.calm_since
                if calm >= c["leave_secs"]:
                    self.level -= 1
                    self.calm_since = None
                    if self.level == 0:
                        self.reason = "all signals low"
                    else:
                        self.reason = (
                            "; ".join(hot[self.level])
                            or f"calm for {calm:.0f} s, down from pause"
                        )
                else:
                    self.reason = f"calm for {calm:.0f} of {c['leave_secs']:.0f} s"
        else:
            pending = hot[2] or hot[1]
            self.reason = (
                "rising: " + "; ".join(pending) if pending else "all signals low"
            )
        if self.level != old:
            self.since = now
            return LEVELS[old]
        return None

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ output

    def write_atomic(self, path: Path, text: str) -> None:
        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=path.parent, prefix=f".{path.name}.")
        try:
            with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
                f.write(text)
            os.replace(tmp, path)
        except BaseException:
            Path(tmp).unlink(missing_ok=True)
            raise

    def level_line(self, now: float, s: dict[str, float | str]) -> str:
        reason = self.reason.replace('"', "'")[:160]
        return (
            f"level={LEVELS[self.level]} since={int(self.since)} updated={int(now)} "
            f'reason="{reason}" top={s["top"]}\n'
        )

    def signals_text(self, s: dict[str, float | str]) -> str:
        return (
            f"mem_full10={s['mem_full']:.2f} scope_some10={s['scope_some']:.2f} "
            f"scope_full10={s['scope_full']:.2f} scope_full_n={s['scope_full_n']} "
            f"top={s['top']} io_full10={s['io_full']:.2f} "
            f"swapin_ps={s['swapin']:.0f} zswpin_ps={s['zswpin']:.0f} "
            f"swapout_ps={s['swapout']:.0f} "
            f"majfault_ps={s['majfault']:.0f} zswpwb_ps={s['zswpwb']:.0f} "
            f"mem_avail_gib={s['mem_avail_gib']:.1f} swap_used_gib={s['swap_used_gib']:.1f} "
            f"swap_room_gib={s['swap_room_gib']:.1f} "
            f"slice_swap={s['slice_swap']}:{float(s['slice_swap_pct']):.0f}%"
        )

    def log(self, now: float, text: str) -> None:
        self.state_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        stamp = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z", time.localtime(now))
        with open(self.log_file, "a") as f:
            f.write(f"{stamp} {text}\n")
        try:
            size = self.log_file.stat().st_size
        except OSError:
            return
        if size > self.cfg["log_max_bytes"]:
            with open(self.log_file, "rb") as f:
                f.seek(size // 2)
                f.readline()
                rest = f.read()
            self.write_atomic(self.log_file, rest.decode(errors="replace"))

    def update_hold(self, now: float) -> None:
        if self.level == 2:
            ttl = int(self.cfg["hold_ttl_secs"])
            self.write_atomic(
                self.hold_file,
                f"expires={int(now) + ttl} pressure-coordinator: level pause ({self.reason[:160]})\n",
            )
        else:
            self.hold_file.unlink(missing_ok=True)

    def tick(self, now: float, mono: float | None = None) -> None:
        mono = now if mono is None else mono
        s = self.sample(mono)
        old = self.step(mono, s, now)
        self.write_atomic(self.level_file, self.level_line(now, s))
        self.update_hold(now)
        if old is not None:
            self.log(
                now,
                f'event=level from={old} to={LEVELS[self.level]} reason="{self.reason}" '
                + self.signals_text(s),
            )
        if mono - self.last_sample_log >= self.cfg["sample_log_secs"]:
            self.last_sample_log = mono
            self.log(
                now,
                f'event=sample level={LEVELS[self.level]} reason="{self.reason}" '
                + self.signals_text(s),
            )

    def shutdown(self) -> None:
        """Leaves the level file and the pressure hold as they are. A restart
        takes them over (resume); after a real stop the hold runs out at its
        expires= (hold_ttl_secs) and heavy-build treats the old level file as
        slow for 10 min. Only a real drop of the level removes the hold."""


def default_paths() -> tuple[Path, Path, Path, Path, Path]:
    home = Path.home()
    uid = os.getuid()
    state = Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME", home / ".local/state")) / "pressure"
    run = Path(os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR", f"/run/user/{uid}"))
    conf = (
        Path(os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME", home / ".config"))
        / "pressure-coordinator.conf"
    )
    usvc = Path(f"/sys/fs/cgroup/user.slice/user-{uid}.slice/user@{uid}.service")
    return Path("/proc"), usvc, state, run, conf


def load_conf(co: Coordinator, conf: Path, now: float) -> None:
    """Reads conf into co.cfg. A file with a bad value is rejected as a
    whole and logged; co.cfg (the last good config) stays."""
    cfg, errs = read_conf(conf)
    if errs:
        co.log(now, f'event=conf-rejected errors="{"; ".join(errs)[:300]}"')
        return
    co.cfg = cfg


def run_forever() -> int:
    proc, usvc, state, run, conf = default_paths()
    co = Coordinator(dict(DEFAULTS), proc, usvc, state, run)
    stop = False

    def on_term(_sig: int, _frame: object) -> None:
        nonlocal stop
        stop = True

    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, on_term)
    signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, on_term)
    now = time.time()
    load_conf(co, conf, now)
    co.since = now
    co.log(now, "event=start " + co.resume(now))
    conf_mtime: float | None = None
    try:
        conf_mtime = conf.stat().st_mtime
    except OSError:
        conf_mtime = 0.0
    while not stop:
        now = time.time()
        mono = time.monotonic()
        try:
            m = conf.stat().st_mtime
        except OSError:
            m = 0.0
        if m != conf_mtime:
            conf_mtime = m
            load_conf(co, conf, now)
        try:
            co.tick(now, mono)
        except Exception as e:  # keep running; a bad sample must not stop the brake
            try:
                co.log(now, f'event=error error="{type(e).__name__}: {e}"')
            except OSError:
                pass
        end = mono + co.cfg["interval"]
        while not stop and time.monotonic() < end:
            time.sleep(min(0.5, max(0.0, end - time.monotonic())))
    co.shutdown()
    co.log(
        time.time(),
        f"event=stop level={LEVELS[co.level]} (level file and hold left for a restart)",
    )
    return 0


def run_once() -> int:
    proc, usvc, state, run, conf = default_paths()
    co = Coordinator(
        read_conf(conf)[0],
        proc,
        usvc,
        Path(tempfile.mkdtemp()),
        Path(tempfile.mkdtemp()),
    )
    co.sample(time.monotonic())
    time.sleep(5)
    mono = time.monotonic()
    s = co.sample(mono)
    co.step(mono, s, time.time())
    print(co.signals_text(s))
    print("raw slow triggers:", co.triggers(s, 1) or "none")
    print("raw pause triggers:", co.triggers(s, 2) or "none")
    for d in (co.state_dir, co.hold_file.parent):
        shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- self-test


def self_test() -> int:
    base = Path(os.environ.get("TMPDIR", "/var/tmp"))
    root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="pc-test.", dir=base))
    fails = 0
    try:
        proc, usvc, state, run = (
            root / "proc",
            root / "usvc",
            root / "state",
            root / "run",
        )
        for d in (proc / "pressure", state, run):
            d.mkdir(parents=True)
        for sl in SLICES:
            (usvc / sl).mkdir(parents=True)
        chrome = usvc / "app.slice/app-chrome.service"
        sess = usvc / "claude.slice/claude-1.scope"
        for d in (chrome, sess):
            d.mkdir()
        vm = {"pswpin": 0, "pswpout": 0, "pgmajfault": 0, "zswpwb": 0, "zswpin": 0}

        def setp(path: Path, some: float, full: float) -> None:
            path.write_text(
                f"some avg10={some:.2f} avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=1\n"
                f"full avg10={full:.2f} avg60=0.00 avg300=0.00 total=1\n"
            )

        def world(
            mem_full: float = 0.0,
            avail_gib: float = 30,
            swap_total_gib: float = 256,
            swap_used_gib: float = 10,
            chrome_full: float = 0.0,
            chrome_high: float = 0,
            sess_some: float = 0.0,
            sess_full: float = 0.0,
            swapin_add: float = 0,
        ) -> None:
            setp(proc / "pressure/memory", mem_full, mem_full)
            setp(proc / "pressure/io", 0, 0)
            vm["pswpin"] += int(swapin_add)
            (proc / "vmstat").write_text("".join(f"{k} {v}\n" for k, v in vm.items()))
            kib = 1048576
            (proc / "meminfo").write_text(
                f"MemAvailable: {int(avail_gib * kib)} kB\n"
                f"SwapTotal: {int(swap_total_gib * kib)} kB\n"
                f"SwapFree: {int((swap_total_gib - swap_used_gib) * kib)} kB\n"
            )
            setp(chrome / "memory.pressure", chrome_full, chrome_full)
            (chrome / "memory.events").write_text(
                f"low 0\nhigh {int(chrome_high)}\nmax 0\noom 0\n"
            )
            setp(sess / "memory.pressure", sess_some, sess_full)
            (sess / "memory.events").write_text("low 0\nhigh 0\nmax 0\noom 0\n")

        def check(name: str, ok: bool, extra: str = "") -> None:
            nonlocal fails
            print(
                ("ok: " if ok else "FAIL: ") + name + (f" ({extra})" if extra else "")
            )
            if not ok:
                fails += 1

        def fresh() -> Coordinator:
            for p in (
                state / "level",
                state / "log",
                run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure",
            ):
                p.unlink(missing_ok=True)
            return Coordinator(dict(DEFAULTS), proc, usvc, state, run)

        def lvl(co: Coordinator) -> str:
            return LEVELS[co.level]

        def run_for(co: Coordinator, t: float, secs: float, **w: float) -> float:
            end = t + secs
            while t < end:
                t += 5
                world(**w)
                co.tick(t)
            return t

        # 1. Calm machine: normal, level file in the agreed format, no hold.
        co = fresh()
        t = run_for(co, 1000.0, 30)
        line = (state / "level").read_text()
        check("calm: level normal", lvl(co) == "normal")
        check(
            "level file: one line, level= since= updated= reason= top=",
            re.fullmatch(
                r'level=normal since=\d+ updated=1030 reason="[^"]*" top=\S+\n', line
            )
            is not None,
            line.strip(),
        )
        check(
            "level file: no temp file left",
            [p.name for p in state.iterdir() if p.name.startswith(".")] == [],
        )
        check(
            "calm: no pressure hold", not (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").exists()
        )

        # 2. Memory full 3% enters slow only after 15 s.
        t = run_for(co, t, 10, mem_full=3)
        check("mem full 3% for 10 s: still normal", lvl(co) == "normal")
        t = run_for(co, t, 10, mem_full=3)
        check("mem full 3% for 20 s: slow", lvl(co) == "slow", co.reason)
        check(
            "slow: transition logged",
            "event=level from=normal to=slow" in (state / "log").read_text(),
        )
        check(
            "slow: no pressure hold", not (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").exists()
        )

        # 3. Memory full 6% for 15 s with 8 GiB available: pause, and the
        # pressure hold is written.
        t = run_for(co, t, 20, mem_full=6, avail_gib=8)
        hold = (
            (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").read_text()
            if lvl(co) == "pause"
            else ""
        )
        check("mem full 6%: pause", lvl(co) == "pause", co.reason)
        check(
            "pause: hold file has expires=now+30 and the reason",
            hold.startswith(
                f"expires={int(t) + 30} pressure-coordinator: level pause (memory full avg10 6.0%"
            ),
            hold.strip(),
        )
        check(
            "pause: the manager's hold file is not touched",
            not (run / "heavy-build.hold").exists(),
        )

        # 4. Leave one level at a time, each after 60 s of calm.
        t = run_for(co, t, 60, mem_full=3, avail_gib=8)
        check(
            "mem full 3% (over half of 5): still pause", lvl(co) == "pause", co.reason
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 50, mem_full=1.5)
        check("calm 50 s: still pause", lvl(co) == "pause", co.reason)
        t = run_for(co, t, 15, mem_full=1.5)
        check("calm 60 s: down to slow", lvl(co) == "slow", co.reason)
        check(
            "down to slow: pressure hold removed",
            not (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").exists(),
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 125, mem_full=0.5)
        check("slow, calm 60 s: back to normal", lvl(co) == "normal", co.reason)

        # 5. A unit at its own MemoryHigh is not machine pressure.
        co = fresh()
        world()
        co.tick(2000.0)
        hi = 0
        t = 2000.0
        for _ in range(12):
            hi += 5
            t = run_for(co, t, 5, chrome_full=60, chrome_high=hi)
        check(
            "Chrome at its own MemoryHigh, full 60%: stays normal",
            lvl(co) == "normal",
            co.reason,
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 90, chrome_full=60, chrome_high=hi)
        check(
            "its high counter still for 60 s: now it counts, but one scope is only slow",
            lvl(co) == "slow",
            co.reason,
        )
        t = run_for(
            co, t, 30, chrome_full=60, chrome_high=hi, sess_some=60, sess_full=60
        )
        check(
            "two scopes at full 60% for 30 s: pause",
            lvl(co) == "pause" and "2 scopes" in co.reason,
            co.reason,
        )

        # 6. A session scope stalling counts.
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 3000.0, 25, sess_some=12)
        check(
            "session some 12% for 25 s: slow, named",
            lvl(co) == "slow" and "claude-1.scope" in co.reason,
            co.reason,
        )

        # 7. Swap room under 12 GiB: pause at once.
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 4000.0, 5, swap_total_gib=100, swap_used_gib=80)
        check(
            "swap room 10 GiB: pause on the first sample", lvl(co) == "pause", co.reason
        )
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 4500.0, 20, swap_total_gib=100, swap_used_gib=70)
        check("swap room 20 GiB for 20 s: slow", lvl(co) == "slow", co.reason)

        # 8. Disk swap-in rate.
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 5000.0, 30, swapin_add=5000)
        check("1000 swap-in pages/s: normal", lvl(co) == "normal", co.reason)
        run_for(co, 5030.0, 60, swapin_add=15000)
        check(
            "3000 swap-in pages/s over the window: slow", lvl(co) == "slow", co.reason
        )

        # 9. MemAvailable under 2 GiB: pause after 15 s.
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 6000.0, 20, avail_gib=1.5)
        check("MemAvailable 1.5 GiB: pause", lvl(co) == "pause", co.reason)
        co.shutdown()
        check(
            "shutdown: the pressure hold stays for a restart (it runs out by itself)",
            (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").exists(),
        )
        # 9b. recover_mem_avail_gib sets the bar for leaving pause (2026-10-26).
        co = fresh()
        t = run_for(co, 6100.0, 20, avail_gib=1.5)
        t = run_for(co, t, 70, avail_gib=3.5)
        check(
            "recover 0: MemAvailable 3.5 GiB (under twice 2) for 70 s: stays pause",
            lvl(co) == "pause" and "still over half: MemAvailable 3.5" in co.reason,
            co.reason,
        )
        co = fresh()
        co.cfg["recover_mem_avail_gib"] = 2.5
        t = run_for(co, 6300.0, 20, avail_gib=1.5)
        t = run_for(co, t, 30, avail_gib=2.2)
        check(
            "recover 2.5: MemAvailable 2.2 GiB: stays pause, reason names the bar",
            lvl(co) == "pause"
            and "under the recovery bar: MemAvailable 2.2 GiB, needs 2.5" in co.reason
            and "still over half" not in co.reason,
            co.reason,
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 70, avail_gib=3.5)
        check(
            "recover 2.5: MemAvailable 3.5 GiB for 70 s: down from pause",
            lvl(co) != "pause",
            co.reason,
        )

        # 10. Config file: numbers win, bad lines are skipped.
        conf = root / "pc.conf"
        conf.write_text("slow_mem_full = 1.5  # note\nbogus=1\npause_mem_full=x\n\n")
        cfg, errs = read_conf(conf)
        check("conf: slow_mem_full=1.5 read", cfg["slow_mem_full"] == 1.5)
        check(
            "conf: a value that is not a number is a problem", len(errs) == 1, str(errs)
        )
        conf.write_text("slow_mem_full = 1.5\nbogus=1\n")
        cfg, errs = read_conf(conf)
        check("conf: unknown keys are skipped, no problem", errs == [], str(errs))
        for bad in ("nan", "inf", "-1", "-inf"):
            conf.write_text(f"pause_mem_full={bad}\n")
            _, errs = read_conf(conf)
            check(f"conf: pause_mem_full={bad} is rejected", len(errs) >= 1, str(errs))
        for bad in (
            "interval=0",
            "interval=0.2",
            "hold_ttl_secs=0",
            "hold_ttl_secs=900",
            "rate_window_secs=0",
        ):
            conf.write_text(bad + "\n")
            _, errs = read_conf(conf)
            check(f"conf: {bad} is rejected", len(errs) >= 1, str(errs))
        conf.write_text("slow_io_full=0\n")
        _, errs = read_conf(conf)
        check("conf: 0 still turns a threshold off", errs == [], str(errs))
        co = fresh()
        co.cfg["slow_mem_full"] = 1.5
        conf.write_text("slow_mem_full=3\ninterval=nan\n")
        load_conf(co, conf, 7500.0)
        check(
            "conf: a bad reload keeps the last good config and is logged",
            co.cfg["slow_mem_full"] == 1.5
            and co.cfg["interval"] == 5
            and "event=conf-rejected" in (state / "log").read_text(),
        )
        conf.write_text("slow_mem_full=3\n")
        load_conf(co, conf, 7501.0)
        check("conf: a good reload is taken", co.cfg["slow_mem_full"] == 3)

        # 11. Log cap.
        co = fresh()
        co.cfg["log_max_bytes"] = 2000
        for i in range(100):
            co.log(7000.0 + i, f"event=sample n={i} " + "x" * 40)
        size = (state / "log").stat().st_size
        tail = (state / "log").read_text().splitlines()[-1]
        check("log: stays under about the cap", size <= 2100, str(size))
        check("log: keeps the newest line", "n=99 " in tail)

        # 13. Restart: take over a level written less than 60 s ago.
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 8000.0, 20, mem_full=6, avail_gib=8)
        check("restart setup: pause", lvl(co) == "pause", co.reason)
        co.shutdown()
        co2 = Coordinator(dict(DEFAULTS), proc, usvc, state, run)
        what = co2.resume(8040.0)
        check("restart 20 s later: takes over pause", lvl(co2) == "pause", what)
        check(
            "restart: the pressure hold is still there",
            (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").exists(),
        )
        world(mem_full=6, avail_gib=8)
        co2.tick(8045.0)
        check(
            "restart: first sample at pause refreshes the hold",
            (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").read_text().startswith("expires=8075 "),
        )
        co3 = Coordinator(dict(DEFAULTS), proc, usvc, state, run)
        what = co3.resume(8045.0 + 61)
        check(
            "restart 61 s after the last update: starts at normal",
            lvl(co3) == "normal",
            what,
        )
        co4 = Coordinator(dict(DEFAULTS), proc, usvc, state, run)
        what = co4.resume(8045.0 - 60)
        check(
            "restart with updated= in the future: stale, normal",
            lvl(co4) == "normal" and "future" in what,
            what,
        )
        co5 = fresh()
        what = co5.resume(9000.0)
        check("restart with no level file: normal", lvl(co5) == "normal", what)

        # 14. A gap between samples starts the calm count again.
        co = fresh()
        t = run_for(co, 10000.0, 20, mem_full=6, avail_gib=8)
        check("gap setup: pause", lvl(co) == "pause")
        t = run_for(co, t, 10, mem_full=1)
        t += 300
        world(mem_full=1)
        co.tick(t)
        check(
            "300 s gap after 10 s of calm: still pause, calm count restarted",
            lvl(co) == "pause" and co.calm_since == t,
            co.reason,
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 125, mem_full=1)
        check("then 125 s of calm samples: slow", lvl(co) == "slow", co.reason)

        # 15. No drop while a higher level's trigger holds.
        co = fresh()
        t = run_for(co, 11000.0, 20, mem_full=3)
        check("higher-trigger setup: slow", lvl(co) == "slow")
        t = run_for(co, t, 10, avail_gib=1.5)
        check(
            "slow, calm otherwise, MemAvailable 1.5 GiB for 10 s: no drop, calm not counted",
            lvl(co) == "slow" and co.calm_since is None,
            co.reason,
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 10, avail_gib=1.5)
        check("and after 15 s it goes to pause", lvl(co) == "pause", co.reason)

        # 16. Monotonic time: a wall clock jump does not move the timers.
        co = fresh()
        world(mem_full=3)
        co.tick(12000.0, 500.0)
        world(mem_full=3)
        co.tick(12000.0 + 3600, 505.0)
        check(
            "wall clock jumps an hour, 5 s monotonic: still normal",
            lvl(co) == "normal",
            co.reason,
        )
        for i in range(3):
            world(mem_full=3)
            co.tick(15605.0 + 5 * i, 510.0 + 5 * i)
        check("20 s monotonic at 3%: slow", lvl(co) == "slow", co.reason)
        check(
            "level file updated= is wall time",
            "updated=15615 " in (state / "level").read_text(),
        )

        # 17. zswpin is logged; slice swap near its max pauses at once.
        co = fresh()
        vm["zswpin"] = 0
        run_for(co, 13000.0, 10)
        log = (state / "log").read_text()
        check(
            "log: zswpin_ps next to swapin_ps",
            "zswpin_ps=" in log and "swapin_ps=" in log,
        )
        bs = usvc / "builds.slice"
        bs.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        (bs / "memory.swap.max").write_text(f"{32 * GIB}\n")
        (bs / "memory.swap.current").write_text(f"{int(29.5 * GIB)}\n")
        (usvc / "claude.slice/memory.swap.max").write_text("max\n")
        (usvc / "claude.slice/memory.swap.current").write_text(f"{100 * GIB}\n")
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 14000.0, 5)
        check(
            "builds.slice swap 29.5 of 32 GiB (92%): pause on the first sample",
            lvl(co) == "pause" and "builds.slice" in co.reason,
            co.reason,
        )
        (bs / "memory.swap.current").write_text(f"{20 * GIB}\n")
        co = fresh()
        run_for(co, 15000.0, 30)
        check(
            "builds.slice swap 20 of 32 GiB, claude.slice max: normal",
            lvl(co) == "normal",
            co.reason,
        )
        for p in ("memory.swap.max", "memory.swap.current"):
            (bs / p).unlink()
            (usvc / "claude.slice" / p).unlink()

        # 18. Memory full with plenty available caps at slow (2026-10-22).
        co = fresh()
        t = run_for(co, 16000.0, 60, mem_full=12, avail_gib=25)
        check(
            "mem full 12%, 25 GiB free for 60 s: slow, not pause, reason says capped",
            lvl(co) == "slow"
            and "memory full avg10 12.0% but 25 GiB free, capped at slow" in co.reason,
            co.reason,
        )
        check(
            "capped: no pressure hold",
            not (run / "heavy-build.hold.pressure").exists(),
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 20, mem_full=12, avail_gib=9.5)
        check(
            "then MemAvailable 9.5 GiB (under 10) for 20 s: pause",
            lvl(co) == "pause" and "memory full avg10 12.0%" in co.reason,
            co.reason,
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 130, mem_full=4, avail_gib=15)
        check(
            "pause, mem full 4% with 15 GiB (under twice 10): stays pause",
            lvl(co) == "pause",
            co.reason,
        )
        t = run_for(co, t, 125, mem_full=4, avail_gib=25)
        check(
            "pause, mem full 4% with 25 GiB: down to slow after 60 s",
            lvl(co) == "slow",
            co.reason,
        )
        co = fresh()
        co.cfg["pause_mem_full_avail_gib"] = 0
        run_for(co, 16500.0, 20, mem_full=6, avail_gib=25)
        check(
            "pause_mem_full_avail_gib=0 turns the cap off: pause at 25 GiB",
            lvl(co) == "pause",
            co.reason,
        )

        # 12. Never signals anything: no kill calls in this file.
        src = Path(__file__).read_text()
        code = src.split("def self_test")[0]
        bad = re.findall(
            r"os\.kill|killpg|subprocess|cgroup\.freeze|cgroup\.kill|memory\.high\b.*write",
            code,
        )
        check("source: no kill, killpg, subprocess or cgroup writes", not bad, str(bad))
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)
    print("all ok" if not fails else f"{fails} failed")
    return 1 if fails else 0


def main() -> int:
    if "--self-test" in sys.argv[1:]:
        return self_test()
    if "--once" in sys.argv[1:]:
        return run_once()
    if sys.argv[1:]:
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[1], file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    return run_forever()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
